Q3(a): Define Stack ADT. Explain array implementation of Stack with push(), pop(), display().

[Student Hand-Written Response]:
Stack is LIFO linear list.
• Push: Check if top == MAX - 1 (Overflow). top++; stack[top] = item;
• Pop: Check if top == -1 (Underflow). item = stack[top]; top--; return item;

Q5(a): Singly Linked List C functions for insertion and deletion at front and end.

[Student Hand-Written Response]:
Node struct: struct Node { int data; struct Node* next; };
• Insert Front: temp->next = head; head = temp;
• Delete Front: temp = head; head = head->next; free(temp);
